{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789836052,"nonce":"jCcXdFY73euI+u2g49VpIXFidEw=","title":"CI benchmarks: tiered binarytrees never left Interpreted since cc70fe31 -- a runtime symbol the compiler emits was not in the plugin inventory","message":"`bench (binarytrees)`: `[FAIL] rayzor-tiered: binarytrees never left Interpreted after 200 iterations` (and precompiled-tiered) on every Benchmarks run from cc70fe31 (00:16) on; 56bee624 (23:44) still promoted (`promote_target func=5 tier=maximum count=2`). The job itself stays green, so only the artifact shows it.\n\ncc70fe31 made every class register its toString through `haxe_type_register_to_string`. The runtime function exists and `rayzor run` binds it, but the benchmark runner builds its `TieredBackend::with_symbols` from `plugin.runtime_symbols()` -- the `register_symbol!` inventory -- which had no entry for it. A module naming an unbound symbol never gets its Maximum-tier body, and the runner reports only \"never left Interpreted\".\n\nFourteen compiler-emitted runtime functions were missing from the inventory (haxe_type_register_to_string, haxe_enum_to_string[_boxed], haxe_bytes_of_int_array, haxe_bytes_get_data, haxe_dynamic_is_null, haxe_null_*_eq x4, haxe_string_concat_ptr, haxe_channel_unbox_erased/try, rayzor_mem_release_free_pages); all registered now. Local check: `./target/release/examples/benchmark_runner binarytrees --single-target rayzor-tiered --disable-trace`.\n\nOpen: the tiered backend should say which symbol failed to bind instead of leaving the function interpreted; `RAYZOR_PROFILE_TIER_EVENTS=1` printed nothing for this failure. A test that diffs `pub extern \"C\" fn` names the compiler emits against the inventory would have caught it at commit time.","files":null}]}